REQUIRES: linux
With trace-args and trace-ret, and nothing else that depends on the input
instrumented, the values reported become value-profile features: inputs that
give Fold() new argument, pointee or return values are new coverage under
-use_value_profile=1 - hundreds of them - while without it only the few new
edges of a longer input are.
RUN: %cpp_compiler -fsanitize-coverage=trace-args,trace-ret -fno-sanitize-coverage=trace-cmp \
RUN:   %S/TraceArgsValueProfileTest.cpp -o %t-TraceArgsValueProfileTest
RUN: %run %t-TraceArgsValueProfileTest -seed=1 -runs=2000 -use_value_profile=1 -use_cmp=0 -print_final_stats=1 2>&1 \
RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=VP
RUN: %run %t-TraceArgsValueProfileTest -seed=1 -runs=2000 -use_value_profile=0 -use_cmp=0 -print_final_stats=1 2>&1 \
RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=NOVP
VP:   stat::new_units_added: {{[1-9][0-9][0-9]+$}}
NOVP: stat::new_units_added: {{[0-3]$}}
